  "summary": "Import-time environment exfiltration to hardcoded third-party webhook",
  "details": "telemetry_helper/__init__.py executes send_ping() at module top level on any `import telemetry_helper`. The function collects hostname, username, current working directory, and the full process environment (dict(os.environ)) and POSTs the payload as JSON to a hardcoded external endpoint at http://ptsv3.com/webhook over plaintext HTTP. Bulk enumeration of os.environ captures credential-grade variables commonly present on developer and CI hosts (AWS_*, GITHUB_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN, database URLs, session tokens). The transport is unencrypted, the destination is a public request-bin service unrelated to the package's declared purpose, and the behavior fires unconditionally without opt-in or configuration.",
